    "text": "{\"anomaly_detected\": true, \"confidence\": 0.85, \"anomalies\": [{\"category\": \"bridged_nets\", \"components\": [\"U6\", \"H8\", \"R3\"], \"pins\": [\"U6.1\", \"H8.4\"], \"nets\": [\"I2C_SDA\", \"/B_{NA}-\"], \"observed\": \"U6 (TMC2209, Nutrient-A driver) pin 1 (OB2, a motor-coil output) and H8 pin 4 (Nutrient-A stepper connector, coil B-) are both on the I2C_SDA net. The /B_{NA}- net that should carry this coil return does not exist. The sibling drivers are wired correctly: U5.1/H7.4 sit on /B_{pH}- and U7.1/H9.4 sit on /B_{NB}-. The main I2C bus SDA line (pulled up by R3 to +3V3, shared with M4, U3.3, U4.3 and the ESP32 IO4) is therefore driven by a stepper coil output and tied to a connector pin.\", \"expected\": \"U6 pin 1 (OB2) and H8 pin 4 should form a separate coil net (/B_{NA}-), mirroring U5/U7. They should not be joined to the non-isolated I2C_SDA bus.\", \"evidence\": [{\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"77\\\") (name \\\"I2C_SDA\\\") (class \\\"Default\\\") ... (node (ref \\\"H8\\\") (pin \\\"4\\\") (pintype \\\"passive\\\")) ... (node (ref \\\"U6\\\") (pin \\\"1\\\") (pinfunction \\\"OB2\\\") (pintype \\\"output\\\")))\"}, {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"31\\\") (name \\\"/B_{pH}-\\\") ... (node (ref \\\"H7\\\") (pin \\\"4\\\") ...) (node (ref \\\"U5\\\") (pin \\\"1\\\") (pinfunction \\\"OB2\\\") ...)\"}, {\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"Netlist: each drives a 2-phase coil output (`/A_xx+/-`, `/B_xx+/-`) to connectors H7/H8/H9\"}, {\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"Netlist: ESP32-C6 pin `IO4/I2C_SDA` \u2192 `I2C_SDA` net; pin `IO5/I2C_SCL` \u2192 `I2C_SCL` net, each pulled up to `+3V3` via 2.2 k\u03a9 resistors (R3, R4).\"}], \"impact\": \"The TMC2209 U6 coil output is shorted to the I2C SDA line. The driver will fight the bus and corrupt I2C traffic to the EZO-RTD, both isolators and any sensors on H5/H6. The Nutrient-A stepper coil also loses its return path, so the pump cannot be driven correctly, and the driver may be damaged.\", \"confidence\": 0.85}], \"summary\": \"The Nutrient-A TMC2209 (U6) coil output OB2 and the H8 coil connector pin 4 are tied to the I2C_SDA bus instead of a dedicated /B_{NA}- net, unlike the U5 and U7 channels. This bridges a motor output onto the main I2C bus and breaks the Nutrient-A coil return.\"}",
